# Everything here is sent to the Docker daemon before the first instruction
# runs, whether or not a COPY ever names it. Without this file the context
# included `.git`, the virtualenv and every generated dataset — hundreds of
# megabytes re-transferred on each build, which on a memory-constrained host is
# the difference between a two-minute rebuild and a twenty-minute one.

# --- version control ---------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# --- local environments ------------------------------------------------------
.venv
venv
# Only the local `.env`. A wider `.env.*` with a `!.env.template` exception
# looks equivalent and is not: the build failed with `"/.env.template": not
# found`, because the Dockerfile copies that file and the exclusion still
# applied to it.
.env

# --- generated data and models -----------------------------------------------
# Regenerated by `monetka demo`; the image mounts `data/` and `artifacts/` from
# the host anyway.
data
artifacts
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
*.parquet
*.onnx
*.tflite

# --- build and test leftovers ------------------------------------------------
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
htmlcov
coverage.xml
*.egg-info
build
dist

# --- dbt --------------------------------------------------------------------
# `dbt_packages` is installed during the build; `target` is compilation output.
transform/dbt_monetka/target
transform/dbt_monetka/dbt_packages
transform/dbt_monetka/logs

# --- documentation -----------------------------------------------------------
# Not read at runtime. `README.md` is the exception: `pyproject.toml` declares
# it as the long description, so the build fails without it.
docs
app-integration
LICENSE
